<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Lakes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Lakes are five large freshwater lakes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> on the border of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. By 1710 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> in North America extended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a> and the St Lawrence through the Great Lakes and down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-lakes.jpg" alt="Great Lakes" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Lakes,_No_Clouds_(4968915002)_Brighter.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
